"text": "This is the most powerful man in Silicon Valley right now, and he's basically Tony Stark in real life. Genius billionaire playboy philanthropist. His name's Palmer Lucky, and the same company that made him a billionaire ended up throwing him out, all over a $10,000 donation he made to a meme page they didn't like. But instead of apologizing or quietly starting another app, he went and did the one thing the whole valley was too squeamish to touch. He started building weapons, autonomous drones that hunt their own targets, the kind that fight real wars. But Palmer's only the side piece. He came out of a company that's quietly turned out some of the most powerful people in tech. A crew everyone now calls the Palantir Mafia. And it all traces back to the godfather of the PayPal Mafia. Teal took the system PayPal built to hunt down fraudsters and aimed it at hunting terrorists instead. That became Palantir. Palantir is here to scare enemies and on occasion kill them. And its first customer was the CIA. Now look at what that crew runs. One builds the weapons, one runs the surveillance state, and one of them quietly took over the accelerator that decides which startups on Earth even get to exist. The PayPal Mafia built the internet you scroll all day. The Palantir Mafia built the thing quietly watching you do it.",
